1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:01,960
Okay, guys, hi.

2
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:04,540
Here's the setup.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,420
I laid it out neatly so you can see there are no shady connections here.

4
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:15,060
Nothing — everything is as usual, basically.

5
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:19,620
Apparently he did it on glass.

6
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:24,540
I'm not going to do glass; I just stuffed the whole rig into an industrial box.

7
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:28,640
This is a low-power generator.

8
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:34,880
You could squeeze a kilowatt out of it, but I'll tell you why I'm not getting a kilowatt from it.

9
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:36,360
For one simple reason.

10
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:38,120
The nanosecond pulse generator is working very weakly.

11
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:40,200
You could excite it harder.

12
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:48,560
I got something out of it, but right now the total power is somewhere between 550 and 600 watts, no more.

13
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:51,500
Plus, if you take into account that I have a diode bridge.

14
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:53,580
Okay, in short.

15
00:00:54,060 --> 00:01:01,560
I deliberately didn't put in any terminal blocks, so you couldn't tell me something's hooked up here.

16
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:03,500
Just a regular twist.

17
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:06,580
There was no other wire, so I twisted this one.

18
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:08,820
I'll show you what's inside now.

19
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:16,040
Here's a terminal block, here's the regular wire screwed in.

20
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:17,460
Nothing special.

21
00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:19,920
The coil.

22
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:23,280
Everyone knows it by heart.

23
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:27,320
Roma, you said there's no inductor here.

24
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:28,780
Yeah, I'll tell you right away — there is one.

25
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:30,920
It's wound underneath along the entire length.

26
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:33,200
Okay, what else?

27
00:01:34,360 --> 00:01:35,760
Regular coaxial cable.

28
00:01:36,860 --> 00:01:39,140
50, well, 75 ohms to be exact.

29
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:41,140
I mean, you can tune any of it.

30
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:45,180
It depends on what capacitor you put in here.

31
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:47,160
Well, there are a couple more wound underneath.

32
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:50,820
Oleg, listen, this core is crap.

33
00:01:51,340 --> 00:01:52,400
Yeah, I mean this ferrite.

34
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:54,720
I need to put the white one back in.

35
00:01:54,820 --> 00:01:56,040
Everything was more powerful with it.

36
00:01:57,440 --> 00:01:58,220
Okay, so what?

37
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:01,580
There's a regular bifilar here.

38
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:02,960
Nothing special.

39
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:05,340
Nothing special, I'm repeating.

40
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:07,620
A two-arm generator.

41
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:14,760
A driving transformer setting the frequency for this converter's operation, where everything happens.

42
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:21,800
Roma, just so you understand — I understand very well what's happening here and why all this works.

43
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:32,440
What's wound around what and why, as they say, there are no resonant caps here, those that I was poking at one time.

44
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:35,020
So, what else?

45
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:42,820
Well, basically 29 turns of wire, and on top there are 12 turns each for these arms.

46
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:49,040
So, synchronization here is bundled with a TL chip — that is, two ICs: driver, TL, driver.

47
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:51,760
All this rig works.

48
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:54,640
Well, this is the converter, the relay block.

49
00:02:55,320 --> 00:03:01,560
One relay cuts the output so it doesn't start up when there's none yet.

50
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:03,960
The high one isn't running.

51
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:06,320
The second relay just clicks the buttons.

52
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:06,480
That's it.

53
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:08,800
So, nothing is happening here.

54
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:13,120
Right now there's no power here whatsoever.

55
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:17,180
Absolutely none — you can measure it if you want.

56
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:25,720
But I really want to sleep, because it's 5 a.m. and I was tinkering until now.

57
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:30,340
And I have to get up at 6, so it's probably better not to lie down at all.

58
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:31,360
Okay.

59
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:35,280
In short, there it is, working.

60
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:38,360
Startup is going.

61
00:03:39,020 --> 00:03:40,940
The generator is running now.

62
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:43,680
The LED is blindingly bright.

63
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:46,000
And the arms are working.

64
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:48,700
It shows that power is being supplied to the arms.

65
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:49,700
It's just LEDs.

66
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:52,640
So, this system isn't working right now.

67
00:03:52,860 --> 00:03:56,140
When I press the button, naturally, everything turns on.

68
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:57,560
Yeah, the power supply.

69
00:03:57,940 --> 00:04:00,120
I mean, of course, the LED is on.

70
00:04:00,260 --> 00:04:02,520
Now everyone's going to ask why it's on.

71
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:03,200
Well, watch.

72
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:04,300
I disconnect the battery.

73
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:06,600
This is for the especially slow.

74
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:07,580
Yeah, see, it went out.

75
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:13,500
Because the power supply is fed from the battery through a diode.

76
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,320
Okay, what next?

77
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:17,460
Alright, we turn it on.

78
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:21,460
As I said, the nanosecond pulse generator will start now.

79
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:23,140
There you go.

80
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:29,560
And immediately the high turns on, and the system rises to full power.

81
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:34,160
I mean, the power supply starts working, calmly putting out 23.5 volts.

82
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:35,740
Well, almost 24.

83
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:38,120
The system is 24-volt.

84
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:39,760
Alright, we've disconnected the battery.

85
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:43,100
What do we get?

86
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:46,100
This is grounding.

87
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:51,700
And this is the wire to the bulb.

88
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:53,700
You've seen the bulbs.

89
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:58,220
Well, that's basically not important.

90
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:00,940
Right, I can't hook up the big ones.

91
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:06,680
Because, alas, this setup just can't handle them.

92
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:10,020
The one you saw in the meadow that time.

93
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:12,940
That setup handled it.

94
00:05:13,460 --> 00:05:15,020
It's been taken apart for now.

95
00:05:15,820 --> 00:05:17,180
In a disassembled state.

96
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:19,460
I mean, I'll restore it later.

97
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:24,980
By the way, the glass cover — notice, there'll be a glass cover here.

98
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:26,760
I don't want to flip it now, the bolts will fly off.

99
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:35,320
There, this is all for those who don't believe anything can work here.

100
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:38,840
Well, that's how it is.

101
00:05:41,270 --> 00:05:43,210
Anyway, in short, here it is working.

102
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:45,530
All this stuff.

103
00:05:47,570 --> 00:05:52,550
Take another look, if you want to count the turns on the coils.

104
00:05:53,670 --> 00:05:54,690
You can count.

105
00:05:55,690 --> 00:05:56,710
There's nothing there.

106
00:05:57,650 --> 00:06:01,490
I won't bring it close — the camera goes nuts from this nanosecond pulse generator.

107
00:06:01,630 --> 00:06:02,890
Sometimes it just shuts down.

108
00:06:03,050 --> 00:06:04,930
I'm exhausted recording videos.

109
00:06:05,030 --> 00:06:06,070
I've already tried twice.

110
00:06:06,890 --> 00:06:08,610
You bring it close and that's it, goodbye.

111
00:06:08,750 --> 00:06:11,530
The camera shuts off, dies, and says the batteries are dead.

112
00:06:11,750 --> 00:06:14,950
Although the batteries, the cells, are charged.

113
00:06:16,330 --> 00:06:20,170
There, I mean, everything, please, everything works.

114
00:06:21,170 --> 00:06:22,050
Everything's great.

115
00:06:23,410 --> 00:06:25,550
Right, no resonant capacitors.

116
00:06:25,550 --> 00:06:28,670
The capacitors here are used for smoothing the power.

117
00:06:30,130 --> 00:06:36,230
As they say, soaking up interference, so as not to pick up everything else — it works.

118
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:39,850
By the way, this system is very similar to Kapanadze's.

119
00:06:40,030 --> 00:06:46,290
I mean, as I already mentioned, what we have here and Kapanadze are practically the same thing.

120
00:06:46,910 --> 00:06:47,930
Look, the bulbs are on.

121
00:06:48,830 --> 00:06:52,090
They're not at full brightness, but they're decent.

122
00:06:53,170 --> 00:06:53,990
Well, what does 'full' mean?

123
00:06:53,990 --> 00:06:57,430
Almost full brightness, you could say.

124
00:06:58,310 --> 00:07:00,310
I don't know, of course I could measure the power.

125
00:07:01,610 --> 00:07:03,690
Basically, I could measure the power.

126
00:07:06,010 --> 00:07:07,730
Okay, we won't do it today.

127
00:07:09,350 --> 00:07:10,310
Such is the deal.

128
00:07:12,170 --> 00:07:12,930
Hi to Oleg.

129
00:07:13,190 --> 00:07:15,050
Next time pick up the phone when someone calls.

130
00:07:16,130 --> 00:07:18,990
I wanted to show you, but…

131
00:07:19,530 --> 00:07:21,870
I mean Oleg who lives in Latvia.

132
00:07:22,950 --> 00:07:25,170
So that's that, well…

133
00:07:25,170 --> 00:07:26,050
That's how the cookie crumbles.

134
00:07:26,150 --> 00:07:27,470
I'll be making another one now.

135
00:07:28,090 --> 00:07:30,270
A machine I'm working on with us.

136
00:07:30,630 --> 00:07:33,630
Working on its assembly.

137
00:07:34,390 --> 00:07:37,050
I'll show you later.

138
00:07:37,950 --> 00:07:40,570
Alright, good mood to everyone.

139
00:07:41,130 --> 00:07:45,010
And most importantly, success in your work.

140
00:07:45,550 --> 00:07:46,310
Bye.
